1
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,590
Come on, everybody
up! Hands in the air!

2
00:01:39,066 --> 00:01:41,262
You back there, pull that
shade. And don't try it!

3
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:43,666
All right, pull those
curtain back there.

4
00:01:43,837 --> 00:01:45,430
Everybody, except the tellers,

5
00:01:45,606 --> 00:01:48,206
put your hands in the air, walk
quickly to the center of the room.

6
00:01:48,342 --> 00:01:50,140
Hands in the air!
Come on, do it right now!

7
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,040
You tell them! One, two.

8
00:01:52,212 --> 00:01:54,477
- Get up there!
- Three. Take three steps back.

9
00:01:54,648 --> 00:01:57,277
Stick your hands in the
top of your pants and skirts.

10
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:59,079
You stay right there.

11
00:01:59,252 --> 00:02:01,585
Hello, Becky. Long time no see.

12
00:02:01,755 --> 00:02:04,715
All right, I want everything in those
four drawers and the safe behind you.

13
00:02:04,858 --> 00:02:05,882
Now!

14
00:02:44,364 --> 00:02:45,593
Cool.

15
00:02:51,204 --> 00:02:52,763
Hey, hey, hey!

16
00:02:53,373 --> 00:02:54,534
Don't try it, my friend.

17
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:58,005
Come on, Willie, let's go!

18
00:03:01,782 --> 00:03:03,978
Come on, come on, come on.

19
00:03:06,153 --> 00:03:07,177
Stay out of it.

20
00:03:26,073 --> 00:03:27,803
- On the floor!
- What the hell's going on?

21
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:30,443
So, what have you been doing
with yourself these days, Willie?

22
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:31,890
I'm a farmer. What do you think?

23
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,069
Yeah?

24
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,547
So, what's this Ben Franklin
doing on the floor mat

25
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:38,396
in the back seat of your car?
You're getting sloppy in your old age.

26
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:40,792
Look, I don't know what
you're talking about. I swear it.

27
00:03:40,954 --> 00:03:42,684
Seems like I heard
those exact same words

28
00:03:42,856 --> 00:03:44,976
the last time you knocked
off the Willow Springs Bank.

29
00:03:45,125 --> 00:03:46,286
Who's your partner, Willie?

30
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:48,429
I didn't do it, damn
it! Easy. Come on.

31
00:03:48,595 --> 00:03:50,154
Detective?

32
00:03:52,466 --> 00:03:54,332
- Yeah, you didn't do it.
- Ugh.

33
00:04:04,945 --> 00:04:06,025
- Save your breath.
- Ben...

34
00:04:06,146 --> 00:04:08,445
- I don't wanna hear it.
- I didn't do it this time.

35
00:04:08,615 --> 00:04:10,455
Save your one call to
phone somebody who cares.

36
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:12,449
- I've been set up.
- One time, just one time,

37
00:04:12,619 --> 00:04:15,088
I'd like to walk in this room
and hear somebody say,

38
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:18,987
"I did it. I wasn't framed. I wasn't at
the wrong place at the wrong time.

39
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:22,755
I did it. I'm sorry I did it and I'm
ready to pay the consequences."

40
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:25,057
- Just once.
- Just give me one minute.

41
00:04:25,232 --> 00:04:27,201
That's all I'm asking.

42
00:04:32,139 --> 00:04:34,973
Ben, you haven't
seen me in six years.

43
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:36,474
I'm a changed man.

44
00:04:38,078 --> 00:04:40,877
I realize I said the same thing to
you the last time you defended me.

45
00:04:41,047 --> 00:04:43,539
- For robbing the same bank.
- For robbing the same bank.

46
00:04:43,717 --> 00:04:45,583
And for telling the
people in that same bank

47
00:04:45,752 --> 00:04:49,484
to do exactly what you told the
people to do in the bank six years ago.

48
00:04:49,656 --> 00:04:51,716
- Ben, I...
- Willie, how many bank robbers

49
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:53,918
do you think there are
that yell at the tellers

50
00:04:54,094 --> 00:04:55,653
to put their hands
in their pants?

51
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:58,424
I served my time. I've been doing
community service ever since.

52
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:00,499
I've been a model citizen, Ben.

53
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:04,729
Burn me once, shame on you.
Burn me twice, shame on me.

54
00:05:04,905 --> 00:05:06,897
Let me guess. You
got no alibi, right?

55
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:12,312
Here's a list of good lawyers.

56
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:16,477
Ben, you more than anyone
else know how good I was.

57
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,379
So ask yourself this:

58
00:05:19,019 --> 00:05:21,818
Would I ever commit a
robbery using my own car?

59
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:26,316
Would I ever be so absent-minded
as to leave a stray $100 bill

60
00:05:26,493 --> 00:05:29,520
just lying around in
the back seat of my car?

61
00:05:29,696 --> 00:05:33,030
Would I ever leave a ski
mask I'd just used in a heist

62
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:36,602
in plain view, in
my own backyard?

63
00:05:37,304 --> 00:05:40,172
You know what the
answer is to that, Ben.

64
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:48,448
How long have you
been working as a teller

65
00:05:48,615 --> 00:05:50,709
- at the Willow Spring Bank?
- Almost nine years.

66
00:05:50,884 --> 00:05:53,080
So you were working there
the last time it was robbed

67
00:05:53,253 --> 00:05:56,121
by the defendant and
his partner six years ago?

68
00:05:56,289 --> 00:05:57,552
Yes, I was.

69
00:05:57,724 --> 00:05:59,404
Do you remember the
events of that robbery?

70
00:05:59,559 --> 00:06:00,583
Vividly.

71
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:04,561
Mr. Roach and his partner walked
out of the bathroom wearing ski masks.

72
00:06:04,731 --> 00:06:06,811
Then they told everybody
in the main area of the bank

73
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:08,595
to congregate in a circle.

74
00:06:08,768 --> 00:06:11,067
Then Mr. Roach came
over to my teller window.

75
00:06:11,238 --> 00:06:12,478
What did he instruct you to do?

76
00:06:12,606 --> 00:06:15,405
Well, he had all of the other
tellers take three steps backwards

77
00:06:15,575 --> 00:06:18,101
and place their hands inside
their pants or their skirts.

78
00:06:18,278 --> 00:06:19,837
Inside their pants?

79
00:06:20,013 --> 00:06:22,983
Yeah, it was such a bizarre request.
That's why I remember it so well.

80
00:06:23,149 --> 00:06:25,675
Then he had me collect all the
money from the tellers' drawers,

81
00:06:25,852 --> 00:06:27,411
as well as from the safe.

82
00:06:27,587 --> 00:06:29,886
Ms. Schraven, was there
anything about this latest robbery

83
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:31,991
that was similar to
the one six years ago?

84
00:06:32,158 --> 00:06:33,717
They were identical.

85
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:37,387
The ski masks, the congregating
of people in the center of the room.

86
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:41,296
He even told the tellers to take
exactly three steps backwards

87
00:06:41,468 --> 00:06:43,266
and place their hands
inside their belts.

88
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:46,505
Was there anything
different about this robbery

89
00:06:46,673 --> 00:06:48,273
from the one that
happened six years ago?

90
00:06:48,441 --> 00:06:51,639
Yes. When the bank robber
approached me this time,

91
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:56,681
he smiled and he said, "Hello,
Becky. Long time no see."

92
00:06:56,850 --> 00:06:58,148
He was so arrogant.

93
00:06:58,318 --> 00:06:59,616
Did you recognize that voice?

94
00:06:59,786 --> 00:07:03,154
I'd recognize that voice
with my eyes closed.

95
00:07:03,757 --> 00:07:05,191
It was the defendant's.

96
00:07:08,495 --> 00:07:11,294
Well, when I saw them running
out of the bank with their ski masks,

97
00:07:11,464 --> 00:07:12,830
I knew what had happened.

98
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:14,946
And then what did
you do, Mr. Golding?

99
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:18,902
Well, I started after them but
one man pointed his gun at me.

100
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,700
Do you remember which
hand he was holding his gun in?

101
00:07:21,875 --> 00:07:24,606
Oh, yeah. It was his left hand.

102
00:07:24,778 --> 00:07:27,475
It would be safe to presume that
the man pointing the gun at you

103
00:07:27,647 --> 00:07:29,309
- was left-handed. Yeah. Mm-hm.

104
00:07:29,482 --> 00:07:33,317
Mr. Golding, did you hear any words
exchanged between the bank robbers?

105
00:07:33,486 --> 00:07:34,510
Oh, yeah.

106
00:07:34,688 --> 00:07:38,022
After the first man drew his
gun, the second man yelled,

107
00:07:38,191 --> 00:07:39,831
"Come on, Willie,
let's get out of here."

108
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,320
"Come on, Willie"? You're
certain that's the name you heard?

109
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:45,990
Oh, yeah. I heard it. I
heard it loud and clear.

110
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,464
That's all.

111
00:07:47,834 --> 00:07:48,858
Mr. Matlock?

112
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:51,465
No questions, Your Honor.

113
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:55,040
Then this court stands in
recess until 9:30 Thursday.

114
00:07:58,411 --> 00:08:00,903
Someone did me up good.

115
00:08:01,081 --> 00:08:04,984
If someone did you up,
Willie, they did you up great.

116
00:08:15,628 --> 00:08:17,028
Yes, yes, yes.

117
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:18,460
Hello.

118
00:08:18,631 --> 00:08:20,759
- Uh, you Ben Matlick?
- No, it's Matlock.

119
00:08:20,934 --> 00:08:23,665
No, no, I'm not him. But maybe
I can help you with something.

120
00:08:24,371 --> 00:08:25,532
I don't want your help.

121
00:08:26,406 --> 00:08:28,739
Well, what is it you wanted
to see Mr. Matlock about?

122
00:08:28,908 --> 00:08:31,207
Uh, why don't you get
Mr. Matlock and I'll tell him?

123
00:08:31,811 --> 00:08:33,871
Mr. Matlock is busy.

124
00:08:34,047 --> 00:08:38,143
- Who's here?
- Some kid. I don't know. Whoa, whoa!

125
00:08:38,318 --> 00:08:40,514
My name's Matt and
get your hands off of me.

126
00:08:41,721 --> 00:08:43,519
What's going on?

127
00:08:44,324 --> 00:08:46,623
Did you wanna
talk to me, uh, Matt?

128
00:08:46,793 --> 00:08:51,458
Uh, yeah, but how about in
private? I don't want him to hear.

129
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:53,031
Oh.

130
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:04,077
- How about some peanut butter?
- Uh, how about a cigarette?

131
00:09:04,244 --> 00:09:06,975
How about some peanut butter?

132
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:16,856
- That's all I get?
- That's all I got for you.

133
00:09:17,023 --> 00:09:21,017
I can prove Willie Roach didn't
rob the bank at Willow Springs.

134
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:24,930
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

135
00:09:25,098 --> 00:09:27,624
I was there when
the robbers drove off.

136
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:31,562
What do you want?

137
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:34,065
You got anything sweet?

138
00:09:41,014 --> 00:09:44,746
- I'm listening.
- Well, I ain't talking. Not yet.

139
00:09:45,819 --> 00:09:47,253
Excuse me?

140
00:09:48,054 --> 00:09:51,149
We need to make... We
need to make an arrangement.

141
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:53,293
What kind of arrangement?

142
00:09:53,993 --> 00:09:56,588
I'll tell you everything you need
to know to get Willie Roach off

143
00:09:56,763 --> 00:09:58,698
if you promise to defend my dad.

144
00:09:59,499 --> 00:10:02,333
He just got busted
for stealing cars.

145
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:09,001
You eat my peanut butter, my chips,
drink my milk and then blackmail me?

146
00:10:09,709 --> 00:10:11,473
Dad always says
life wasn't fair.

147
00:10:12,178 --> 00:10:13,646
Look where it got him.

148
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:16,875
How do I know that
you were at the bank?

149
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:18,382
Their car was blue,

150
00:10:18,551 --> 00:10:21,031
it was parked at the first meter
from the driveway of the bank.

151
00:10:21,187 --> 00:10:23,986
And when they drove off, their
bumper clipped the parking meter

152
00:10:24,157 --> 00:10:26,058
as they went away.

153
00:10:26,426 --> 00:10:28,793
So, what do you
say? We got a deal?

154
00:10:35,101 --> 00:10:36,535
Deal.

155
00:11:05,932 --> 00:11:09,733
I am so grateful that you're
helping me out here, Mr. Matlock.

156
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:13,469
- Well, you can, uh, thank your son.
- Yeah.

157
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:16,576
- Good old Matty.
- Yeah, good old Matty.

158
00:11:16,743 --> 00:11:19,110
He says you tend
bar for a living.

159
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:21,145
Yeah. At Plato's Bar and Grill.

160
00:11:21,314 --> 00:11:23,715
Well, what were you
doing at that chop shop

161
00:11:23,883 --> 00:11:25,749
when the police
found those cars?

162
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:29,117
It's not a chop shop,
Mr. Matlock. It's a body shop.

163
00:11:29,289 --> 00:11:32,487
And Mark Lipton has been a
friend of mine since I was a kid.

164
00:11:33,092 --> 00:11:36,551
- Who's Mark Lipton?
- He's the owner.

165
00:11:44,938 --> 00:11:48,204
So, uh, you didn't
steal any of those cars

166
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:51,208
the police found at
your friend's body shop?

167
00:11:51,911 --> 00:11:53,072
No, of course not.

168
00:11:53,813 --> 00:11:57,250
Explain what you were doing
with $2,000 in your pocket

169
00:11:57,417 --> 00:12:00,854
and how your fingerprints got all
over the inside of that stolen Porsche

170
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:02,113
the police impounded.

171
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:04,653
The reason I had the cash

172
00:12:04,824 --> 00:12:07,589
was because Mark had just
paid me back some money

173
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,388
I had loaned to him.

174
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:13,055
And what happened was I got
there and he was with a client.

175
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,327
And I was just killing time.

176
00:12:15,501 --> 00:12:18,096
I saw that beautiful Porsche,

177
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:21,939
and I just wanted to see what
it would be like on the inside.

178
00:12:22,108 --> 00:12:24,873
So I hopped in. Now, that's
what happened, scout's honor.

179
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:26,478
Hmm.

180
00:12:26,646 --> 00:12:31,050
Did you say "scout's honor" the last
time you got busted for stealing cars?

181
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:34,954
That was a long
time ago, Mr. Matlock.

182
00:12:35,121 --> 00:12:36,384
I'm a changed man.

183
00:12:37,023 --> 00:12:39,117
Changed man.

184
00:12:39,292 --> 00:12:40,760
I've heard that before lately.

185
00:12:40,927 --> 00:12:43,920
If I hear it many more times,
I'm gonna toss my cookies.

186
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:45,395
Are you gonna take my case?

187
00:12:45,565 --> 00:12:50,162
I promised your boy I would,
so I'll talk to you in a couple days.

188
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:11,815
Well, how's my dad? I
mean, did you see him?

189
00:13:11,991 --> 00:13:13,084
- Is he all right?
- Okay.

190
00:13:14,527 --> 00:13:16,792
- So are you gonna take his case?
- I told you I would.

191
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:19,990
Now it's your turn. What
did you see at the bank?

192
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:23,500
- Well, first you gotta put up his bail.
- Oh, okay.

193
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:26,640
- Whoa, whoa, where are you going?
- To drop your father's case.

194
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:30,208
All right, listen, you don't
have to pick up his bail.

195
00:13:30,376 --> 00:13:33,778
It's just that I don't wanna
have to have him stay in jail.

196
00:13:33,946 --> 00:13:35,881
You ready to talk?

197
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:39,809
Let's go in the bathroom.

198
00:13:50,096 --> 00:13:52,122
- Well?
- Shh.

199
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,071
I saw the two bank robbers.

200
00:13:59,238 --> 00:14:01,002
What do you mean, "saw"?

201
00:14:01,174 --> 00:14:03,905
When both of them went back to
their car, they took off their masks.

202
00:14:04,077 --> 00:14:07,536
I saw them and neither one of
those guys was Willie Roach.

203
00:14:07,714 --> 00:14:08,738
You're sure?

204
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:11,578
I saw Willie Roach's picture in the
newspaper when he got arrested.

205
00:14:11,751 --> 00:14:12,810
I'm positive.

206
00:14:12,985 --> 00:14:16,149
Matt, if you looked at
some police mug books,

207
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:17,847
do you think you
could pick them out?

208
00:14:18,558 --> 00:14:22,325
- If they're in there, I'll find them.
- Okay. I got court.

209
00:14:22,495 --> 00:14:24,157
I'll set it up
for a little later.

210
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:27,357
Maybe you better go home now.
Your mother might be worried about you.

211
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,161
Uh, my mom is dead.

212
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:32,202
Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't know.

213
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:33,533
Well, where are you staying?

214
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:38,835
- Uh, at my aunt's house.
- Oh. Where is that? I'll give you a lift.

215
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:42,413
Uh, 825 Front Street.

216
00:14:43,149 --> 00:14:45,414
825.

217
00:14:46,419 --> 00:14:50,481
Front Street only goes
up to the 600 block.

218
00:14:50,656 --> 00:14:53,125
I'm sorry, Matt, I can't
let you stay by yourself.

219
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:55,022
I'm not staying at no shelter.

220
00:14:59,632 --> 00:15:02,227
Okay, for now, you
can stay with me.

221
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:04,234
- Cool.
- Okay.

222
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,378
- Mr. Matlock.
- Mr. Matlock, do you think

223
00:15:07,507 --> 00:15:09,066
you're going to get
Roach acquitted?

224
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:10,710
I'd just as soon
not get into that.

225
00:15:10,877 --> 00:15:13,757
But what about the testimony of the
teller and the parking lot attendant?

226
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,033
I'm not gonna get into that.

227
00:15:15,181 --> 00:15:17,501
Does Willie Roach have an
alibi for the day of the robbery?

228
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:19,778
Do you think there's a
copycat robber out there?

229
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:35,363
Pete, Pete, got a second?

230
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:43,103
We got trouble.

231
00:15:45,178 --> 00:15:49,240
That kid with Ben Matlock, that's
the one I saw in the parking lot.

232
00:15:49,415 --> 00:15:52,544
- What did Matlock say?
- I don't know.

233
00:15:53,052 --> 00:15:55,521
That kid saw both of us, Pete.

234
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:08,465
Yeah, this is Pete.
You see the news?

235
00:16:12,672 --> 00:16:14,368
I raise.

236
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:17,567
So you didn't recognize
anyone in those mug shots, huh?

237
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:20,872
- No.
- That's too bad.

238
00:16:21,047 --> 00:16:23,676
Are you gonna talk
or are we gonna play?

239
00:16:25,284 --> 00:16:27,651
I'm gonna fold. I'm
gonna go eat my winnings.

240
00:16:29,322 --> 00:16:32,815
It's five chocolate mints
to you if you wanna stay in.

241
00:16:33,459 --> 00:16:35,018
It's yours.

242
00:16:35,328 --> 00:16:37,559
Now that the
lightweight's gone, uh,

243
00:16:37,730 --> 00:16:39,892
what do you say we
play for some real stakes?

244
00:16:40,066 --> 00:16:41,625
Penny, nickel, dime?

245
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:45,669
What do you say the loser goes
and gets ice cream for the winner?

246
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,431
You're on.

247
00:16:47,974 --> 00:16:49,465
Shuffle them up.

248
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:56,642
There you go.

249
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,079
I feel lucky.

250
00:17:02,922 --> 00:17:04,481
How many?

251
00:17:05,658 --> 00:17:07,889
- Four.
- Oh, one of a kind. Good hand.

252
00:17:16,602 --> 00:17:18,571
I'm gonna take, uh...

253
00:17:20,673 --> 00:17:22,539
I'm gonna take three.

254
00:17:41,193 --> 00:17:42,627
Guess it's show
and tell time, huh?

255
00:17:43,829 --> 00:17:45,889
Well, that's unless
you wanna raise the pot.

256
00:17:46,432 --> 00:17:47,456
To what?

257
00:17:48,534 --> 00:17:51,902
The loser buys ice cream
for everybody in the house.

258
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,404
And it's double scoops.

259
00:17:56,008 --> 00:17:57,704
It's your money.

260
00:18:00,146 --> 00:18:02,047
Three eights.

261
00:18:05,051 --> 00:18:08,021
Three little guys with
little crowns on their heads.

262
00:18:08,187 --> 00:18:09,947
Three kings? Hey, hold
on. You can't do that.

263
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,387
Let me tell you something, Matt.

264
00:18:11,557 --> 00:18:13,838
If you're gonna play by your
own rules, even if you cheat,

265
00:18:13,993 --> 00:18:16,724
there's always gonna be somebody
who does it better than you.

266
00:18:16,896 --> 00:18:18,888
I'll take a double
scoop of chocolate chip.

267
00:18:19,065 --> 00:18:20,328
Cliff likes vanilla.

268
00:18:52,431 --> 00:18:57,267
Hey, forget the kid! Come
on, let's go! Come on!

269
00:18:59,171 --> 00:19:01,367
Go, go, go!

270
00:19:06,112 --> 00:19:10,743
- You all right?
- Yeah. Yeah. I'm fine.

271
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:25,894
So, what was Joe Ahern doing here
the night that the police arrested him?

272
00:19:26,065 --> 00:19:28,625
You mean when the police knocked
down my door and handcuffed me?

273
00:19:28,801 --> 00:19:31,066
Uh, yeah, whatever.
What was he doing here?

274
00:19:31,237 --> 00:19:33,797
I owed him some money.
He came by to pick it up.

275
00:19:33,973 --> 00:19:35,703
- Was that your 2 grand?
- Yeah.

276
00:19:35,875 --> 00:19:38,504
You mind my asking why
you borrowed $2,000 from him?

277
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:42,315
Nothing in particular. Bills.

278
00:19:42,481 --> 00:19:43,847
This look like a
chop shop to you?

279
00:19:44,817 --> 00:19:46,752
I'm really the wrong
person to ask that.

280
00:19:46,919 --> 00:19:50,549
It's infuriating. You try to
run a legitimate business...

281
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:52,956
Why don't you
leave me your card?

282
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:57,324
I'm considering filing an unlawful
arrest suit against the police.

283
00:19:57,496 --> 00:19:59,158
Maybe your firm could handle it.

284
00:19:59,331 --> 00:20:00,765
Why don't we
deal with that later?

285
00:20:00,933 --> 00:20:04,233
Right now I just have to make sure
that Joe Ahern wasn't being paid off

286
00:20:04,403 --> 00:20:07,066
for any business dealings
you might have had with him.

287
00:20:07,239 --> 00:20:11,768
Look, I know you're doing your job,
but these questions, they offend me.

288
00:20:12,511 --> 00:20:15,504
Believe me, you're the last
guy on earth I want to offend.

289
00:20:15,681 --> 00:20:17,309
I know that.

290
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,619
Look, Joe's a bartender.

291
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:20,980
I run a body shop.

292
00:20:21,153 --> 00:20:24,248
What kind of business
dealings could we possibly have?

293
00:20:24,423 --> 00:20:26,756
We're friends, Mr. Lewis.

294
00:20:26,926 --> 00:20:30,761
And that's all we are, friends.

295
00:20:56,055 --> 00:20:58,251
This will just take
a couple minutes.

296
00:20:58,424 --> 00:21:01,019
- Why can't I just stay in the car?
- Well, I told you.

297
00:21:01,193 --> 00:21:02,889
If you're gonna take
the stand for me,

298
00:21:03,062 --> 00:21:06,226
I have to know exactly where you
were when you saw the bank robbers.

299
00:21:06,398 --> 00:21:09,800
- I can tell you from in here.
- Matt, we've been through that before.

300
00:21:09,969 --> 00:21:11,665
- Yeah, yeah.
- Come on.

301
00:21:12,171 --> 00:21:13,571
Come on.

302
00:21:14,874 --> 00:21:17,105
Come on, let's
go. Let's get out.

303
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:20,246
Come on. Come on.

304
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:22,581
Come on.

305
00:21:24,016 --> 00:21:25,746
Okay, here we go.

306
00:21:27,253 --> 00:21:28,414
Hey, hey, hey, you!

307
00:21:28,587 --> 00:21:30,818
- What are you doing here?
- Let's go.

308
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:33,983
- Why are you yelling at the boy?
- The boy is a thief.

309
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:37,597
I caught him four times stealing
things from cars parked in my lot.

310
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:40,665
- He's lying.
- I'm not lying.

311
00:21:44,637 --> 00:21:48,768
So that's what you were doing
when you saw the robbers drive off.

312
00:21:48,941 --> 00:21:50,861
You know what you've
done to Willie Roach's case?

313
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:53,946
You're no good as a witness
anymore. I can't put you on the stand.

314
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:58,346
The DA finds out you were
ripping off cars, he'll tear you apart.

315
00:21:58,818 --> 00:22:00,878
I'll drop your
father's case now.

316
00:22:01,053 --> 00:22:02,112
We made an arrangement.

317
00:22:02,288 --> 00:22:04,888
I said I'd tell you what I knew
about the case. That was our deal.

318
00:22:05,024 --> 00:22:07,016
- I lived up to my part.
- Let's go.

319
00:22:07,193 --> 00:22:08,661
- Where are we going?
- To a shelter.

320
00:22:08,828 --> 00:22:11,229
- I'm not going to no shelter.
- Yes...

321
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:35,787
- Hey.
- Ah.

322
00:22:35,955 --> 00:22:38,754
- What are you doing?
- Pulling weeds.

323
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,322
Doesn't look like much fun.

324
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,988
It's not.

325
00:22:43,896 --> 00:22:45,762
- You mad?
- Yeah.

326
00:22:46,799 --> 00:22:48,165
You're mad that Matt ran away?

327
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:52,033
Why would I be mad about that?

328
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:54,298
- Hi.
- Hi.

329
00:22:56,008 --> 00:22:58,034
What are you doing here?

330
00:22:58,277 --> 00:23:00,712
- We need to talk.
- We don't need to talk.

331
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,349
I packed your stuff. You're
heading for the shelter.

332
00:23:03,515 --> 00:23:05,643
I'm not going to a shelter.

333
00:23:05,818 --> 00:23:07,616
I've been thinking
about the robbery

334
00:23:07,786 --> 00:23:10,017
- and I remember something.
- What?

335
00:23:10,189 --> 00:23:12,181
Well, why don't we
discuss it over coffee?

336
00:23:12,358 --> 00:23:14,725
- Over milk.
- What's wrong with coffee?

337
00:23:14,894 --> 00:23:17,022
You're a kid. We'll
discuss it over milk.

338
00:23:23,168 --> 00:23:28,368
- Some apple pie?
- Yeah, and, uh, more milk.

339
00:23:28,774 --> 00:23:30,333
I'm ready.

340
00:23:30,509 --> 00:23:32,910
- Boy, are you in a bad mood.
- I'm not in a bad mood.

341
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:34,546
I just wanna know
what you remember.

342
00:23:34,713 --> 00:23:37,182
First you gotta promise
you'll defend my father's case.

343
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:40,513
Starting right now, you're living
under a whole new set of rules.

344
00:23:40,686 --> 00:23:43,019
You so much as lie to me
about your temperature,

345
00:23:43,188 --> 00:23:45,623
I drop your father's case
and you go to juvenile hall.

346
00:23:45,791 --> 00:23:47,817
- You are in a bad mood.
- Let's hear it.

347
00:23:49,194 --> 00:23:51,434
You know those stickers they
have for Dynamo Rent-A-Cars?

348
00:23:51,563 --> 00:23:53,088
- Sure.
- Yeah.

349
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:55,359
Well, the thieves' car
was a blue Chevy Lumina.

350
00:23:55,534 --> 00:23:58,504
On the window there was a
Dynamo Rental Car sticker.

351
00:23:59,238 --> 00:24:00,763
It was a rental.

352
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:03,202
You gotta admit now,
that's pretty good.

353
00:24:03,809 --> 00:24:06,802
So, what do you say,
can I have my room back?

354
00:24:08,547 --> 00:24:09,742
Please?

355
00:24:30,936 --> 00:24:33,599
Hey, Matt, what are you doing?

356
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:36,639
This person's car door was open.

357
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:38,243
I was just closing it for them.

358
00:24:43,882 --> 00:24:44,906
Look, I was.

359
00:24:45,751 --> 00:24:48,983
We told you not to come outside
after what happened yesterday.

360
00:24:50,055 --> 00:24:52,388
Oh, yeah. Sorry.

361
00:24:53,392 --> 00:24:56,055
- Wanna go see your dad?
- Yeah, sounds cool.

362
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,260
There you go, Mr. Lewis.

363
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,866
- Thanks, Paul. We'll just be a minute.
- All right.

364
00:25:07,039 --> 00:25:09,719
Hold on. I thought you said you
were gonna take me to see my father.

365
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:11,537
We're gonna go. We'll go.

366
00:25:11,710 --> 00:25:14,407
Ever been inside
a jail cell before?

367
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:17,039
No.

368
00:25:18,083 --> 00:25:19,551
Come on.

369
00:25:24,223 --> 00:25:27,159
Go ahead. Go ahead.

370
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,833
Sit down.

371
00:25:37,636 --> 00:25:42,233
- Can I please go see my dad?
- Oh, just relax. We'll go.

372
00:25:44,009 --> 00:25:47,377
- You like to read?
- No.

373
00:25:48,881 --> 00:25:51,282
- Like to draw?
- No. Can we please go?

374
00:25:51,450 --> 00:25:54,130
Yeah, I know something you like
to do. Poke around in people's cars.

375
00:25:54,286 --> 00:25:55,726
Look, I already
told you, I wasn't...

376
00:25:55,821 --> 00:25:57,756
Hey, please, don't
insult me. All right?

377
00:25:57,923 --> 00:25:59,603
I tell you, you are
lucky you are underage.

378
00:25:59,758 --> 00:26:02,358
Because if you were 18, you got
caught breaking into someone's car

379
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:06,829
or stealing, I don't know, a hubcap, you
know, you'd end up in here for months.

380
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:10,697
- Okay. Can we go now?
- No, no, we can't go now.

381
00:26:15,908 --> 00:26:17,240
Think you're bored now, Matt.

382
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:20,811
Just sitting in here day in and
day out every day with nothing to do.

383
00:26:20,979 --> 00:26:22,859
And you're scared to go
out there. You know why?

384
00:26:23,015 --> 00:26:25,814
Because the guys you gotta eat
with, the guys you gotta shower with,

385
00:26:25,984 --> 00:26:28,977
- they're a lot tougher than you are.
- Yeah, I got it.

386
00:26:29,688 --> 00:26:31,288
You don't really get
to see your friends.

387
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:34,689
You know they are allowed to
come visit you but they don't come.

388
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:35,884
They're embarrassed.

389
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:39,560
You don't really get
to watch a lot of TV.

390
00:26:40,466 --> 00:26:46,804
But I tell you, the worst part is at night
when you're trying to sleep, you can't.

391
00:26:47,172 --> 00:26:50,233
Because all night long there's
one or two guys just screaming

392
00:26:50,409 --> 00:26:53,402
and yelling that
they wanna get out.

393
00:27:04,590 --> 00:27:07,458
All right, now we
can go see your dad.

394
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:35,210
<i>Mr. Kerr, your
foursome is on the tee</i>

395
00:27:35,387 --> 00:27:37,322
<i>and Bridges party to follow.</i>

396
00:27:53,972 --> 00:27:58,239
<i>Bridges party, we have
Mr. Jones to join you.</i>

397
00:28:03,649 --> 00:28:05,083
Jeff.

398
00:28:05,817 --> 00:28:07,376
Yeah, Bonnie?

399
00:28:10,322 --> 00:28:11,620
So, what's up?

400
00:28:11,790 --> 00:28:13,830
Jeff, this is Cliff Lewis
from Ben Matlock's office.

401
00:28:13,992 --> 00:28:15,688
- Oh, yeah, hi.
- Hi, how are you?

402
00:28:15,861 --> 00:28:17,159
Good, good.

403
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:19,924
- Thanks, Bonnie.
- You're welcome.

404
00:28:24,870 --> 00:28:29,365
- If anybody gets her, I do.
- Right. Right.

405
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:31,976
- Thanks for seeing me.
- It's no problem.

406
00:28:32,144 --> 00:28:34,670
You know, I've been thinking
about this since you called

407
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:37,766
and there's nothing I can tell you
that I haven't already told the police.

408
00:28:37,916 --> 00:28:40,356
Just go over it again. We'll see
if we come up with something.

409
00:28:40,485 --> 00:28:42,351
Your Porsche was
stolen from your driveway?

410
00:28:42,521 --> 00:28:43,784
Uh-huh.

411
00:28:43,956 --> 00:28:47,586
The passenger-side door was broken
so I figure that's how the thief got in.

412
00:28:47,759 --> 00:28:49,193
Do you know a guy
named Joe Ahern?

413
00:28:49,761 --> 00:28:51,127
I don't think so.

414
00:28:51,964 --> 00:28:53,804
Do you ever eat at a
restaurant called Plato's?

415
00:28:53,966 --> 00:28:57,198
- It's about two blocks from your office.
- Yeah, yeah, a couple times. Why?

416
00:28:57,369 --> 00:28:59,463
Well, Joe Ahern is
the bartender there.

417
00:28:59,638 --> 00:29:02,198
Oh, well, I don't drink. See, so
I wouldn't have gone in the bar.

418
00:29:02,374 --> 00:29:04,809
Sometimes when I work late, I
go there, get something to eat.

419
00:29:04,977 --> 00:29:07,913
- It's Greek. It's pretty good.
- Mm-hm, mm-hm.

420
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:10,508
Maybe it's all
just a coincidence.

421
00:29:10,682 --> 00:29:13,083
- What?
- Well, your car was stolen.

422
00:29:13,252 --> 00:29:14,276
You eat at Plato's.

423
00:29:14,453 --> 00:29:16,493
And Joe Ahern, the guy
accused of stealing your car?

424
00:29:16,655 --> 00:29:17,714
He works at Plato's.

425
00:29:18,957 --> 00:29:20,152
Yeah.

426
00:29:23,729 --> 00:29:25,163
These people got me down pat.

427
00:29:26,198 --> 00:29:29,259
- It's like they worked with me.
- It's possible.

428
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:30,874
No, the only guy I
ever worked with,

429
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:33,767
Gary Scott's doing 3
to 5 at Atlanta State.

430
00:29:41,847 --> 00:29:43,042
That's amazing.

431
00:29:43,715 --> 00:29:44,944
What?

432
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:47,052
In my life, I've
robbed 27 banks.

433
00:29:47,219 --> 00:29:50,587
Only one time did I have someone
collect the money from the tellers.

434
00:29:50,756 --> 00:29:53,988
It was when I robbed the Willow
Springs Bank six years ago.

435
00:29:54,559 --> 00:29:55,618
How'd they know that?

436
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:58,794
You didn't go to trial
on that robbery, did you?

437
00:29:58,964 --> 00:30:01,593
- No, we cut a deal.
- Ah.

438
00:30:02,968 --> 00:30:07,599
Not a lot of press. Details of
the robbery wouldn't be known.

439
00:30:07,773 --> 00:30:10,902
Only somebody who was in the
bank when you robbed it six years ago

440
00:30:11,076 --> 00:30:13,136
would know what you did.

441
00:30:13,312 --> 00:30:15,907
- Do you think?
- This will play out.

442
00:30:16,081 --> 00:30:18,243
Just take a little time.

443
00:30:39,204 --> 00:30:42,197
- Congratulations.
- For what?

444
00:30:42,374 --> 00:30:44,172
Did you know that
Dynamo Rent-A-Car

445
00:30:44,343 --> 00:30:49,145
has approximately 373
blue Chevy Luminas?

446
00:30:49,314 --> 00:30:52,011
Did you find the car
we're looking for?

447
00:30:53,085 --> 00:30:55,919
You sure have a way of taking
the fun out of my little successes.

448
00:30:56,088 --> 00:30:58,023
Did you find the car?

449
00:30:58,323 --> 00:31:02,158
- You really are in a bad mood.
- Did you find the car?

450
00:31:04,629 --> 00:31:06,860
You know how they
walk around the car

451
00:31:07,032 --> 00:31:10,366
and they check it for little dings
and little dents before you rent it?

452
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:13,937
And then they do the same
thing when you bring it back?

453
00:31:14,973 --> 00:31:18,102
Matt said the car
hit a parking meter.

454
00:31:18,276 --> 00:31:20,472
And on the day of the
robbery, only one blue Lumina

455
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:25,783
was returned with a new
scratch on the front bumper.

456
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:27,849
What is that?

457
00:31:28,687 --> 00:31:30,212
Probably Matt.

458
00:31:30,389 --> 00:31:32,051
Who rented it?

459
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:34,284
Phony license. Phony address.

460
00:31:34,459 --> 00:31:40,330
If you move up the black 4, you can
take your red 5 and put it right there.

461
00:31:43,635 --> 00:31:44,864
Wait a minute.

462
00:31:51,676 --> 00:31:53,304
Matt,

463
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:58,475
this is my house. This is my property.
We don't throw the ball in the house.

464
00:31:59,317 --> 00:32:00,478
Sorry.

465
00:32:00,652 --> 00:32:03,520
You wanna throw
the ball, take it, uh...

466
00:32:03,789 --> 00:32:07,988
- Take it outside.
- He can't go outside.

467
00:32:08,393 --> 00:32:11,261
Yeah, they're trying
to kill him outside.

468
00:32:11,663 --> 00:32:14,064
He may not be safe in the house.

469
00:32:25,177 --> 00:32:27,737
Have you ever had a gun
pointed at you, Miss Stone?

470
00:32:27,913 --> 00:32:29,913
Yeah. Used to happen all
the time when I was a cop.

471
00:32:30,715 --> 00:32:32,877
- Then you know how scary it is.
- Yeah.

472
00:32:33,051 --> 00:32:35,077
I was a nervous wreck
at work the next day.

473
00:32:35,253 --> 00:32:37,085
I've never been
like that before.

474
00:32:37,255 --> 00:32:40,714
I kept thinking someone was
gonna stick a gun in my face.

475
00:32:40,892 --> 00:32:43,487
After about an hour,
I went to see Sarah.

476
00:32:43,662 --> 00:32:45,062
She's the head teller.

477
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:47,529
I told her I have to leave.

478
00:32:47,699 --> 00:32:49,964
I don't think I can work
as a teller anymore.

479
00:32:50,669 --> 00:32:53,605
- It's gotta be tough.
- Yeah.

480
00:32:53,772 --> 00:32:56,571
- Is that all?
- Well, no.

481
00:32:56,741 --> 00:32:59,472
I'm sorry but I'm gonna have to
ask you about the robbery again.

482
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:03,976
We have a witness, a young
boy saw the robbers' faces

483
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:06,914
and he's absolutely sure that
neither one of them was Willie Roach.

484
00:33:07,352 --> 00:33:09,412
- So it's his word against mine?
- Yeah.

485
00:33:09,588 --> 00:33:11,508
That's why we'd like
you to think about it again.

486
00:33:11,656 --> 00:33:14,717
- Maybe you made a mistake.
- No, I didn't make a mistake.

487
00:33:14,893 --> 00:33:16,623
I saw his eyes. He
called me by name.

488
00:33:16,795 --> 00:33:17,819
I'll never forget him.

489
00:33:18,897 --> 00:33:21,093
The robbers have
already tried to kill the boy.

490
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:23,113
We've had to put him into hiding

491
00:33:23,268 --> 00:33:26,102
which makes us think
that he's probably right.

492
00:33:26,271 --> 00:33:27,899
Tried to kill him. I
mean, you're sure?

493
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:33,368
I mean, I could've
sworn it was him.

494
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:36,576
It would be terrible if I
accused the wrong man.

495
00:33:37,382 --> 00:33:39,476
Why don't you think about it?

496
00:33:41,353 --> 00:33:44,846
Thanks. I'll see myself out.

497
00:33:47,125 --> 00:33:49,822
It must have been really scary
having that gun pointed at you.

498
00:33:49,995 --> 00:33:51,691
Yeah.

499
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:55,595
We just wanna make sure
the wrong man doesn't go to jail.

500
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:04,776
I should be back in an hour.

501
00:34:58,330 --> 00:35:00,959
All right, all
right, I'm coming.

502
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:11,140
- What's all this?
- It's my lunch.

503
00:35:11,309 --> 00:35:13,005
I gave you lunch.

504
00:35:13,178 --> 00:35:15,306
You gave me one hot
dog. I was still hungry.

505
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:18,211
You know, they have 24-hour
room service here. You ought to try it.

506
00:35:18,383 --> 00:35:22,878
I had a shrimp cocktail, a
roast beef with mashed potatoes

507
00:35:23,054 --> 00:35:26,547
and a chocolate sundae
with a cherry on top.

508
00:35:26,725 --> 00:35:29,160
I'm going downstairs
and cut you off.

509
00:35:29,327 --> 00:35:31,887
No room service, no
phone calls, no nothing.

510
00:35:32,063 --> 00:35:34,658
You want something, you're
gonna have to pay for it.

511
00:35:34,833 --> 00:35:36,426
I put you here for your safety,

512
00:35:36,601 --> 00:35:40,436
not to have a good time
and break me in the process.

513
00:35:40,605 --> 00:35:43,165
Don't you think
you're overreacting?

514
00:36:10,435 --> 00:36:13,496
- Room service. Pick up.
- It's open.

515
00:36:14,906 --> 00:36:16,340
Drop it! Drop it now!

516
00:36:20,211 --> 00:36:22,373
I wanna see your hands
up there on the wall.

517
00:36:22,547 --> 00:36:24,345
Not that hand, the other one.

518
00:36:24,516 --> 00:36:26,485
Nice job.

519
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:34,314
- Those the guys?
- Those are the guys.

520
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:40,188
<i>Dad, you should've
seen it. It was very cool.</i>

521
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:42,459
When they knocked on
the door, I was very relaxed.

522
00:36:42,634 --> 00:36:44,194
I went up to them,
I said, "It's open."

523
00:36:44,335 --> 00:36:47,135
Then the cops busted down the door
and there they were with their guns.

524
00:36:47,305 --> 00:36:49,586
If the police hadn't been there,
they were gonna shoot me.

525
00:36:49,741 --> 00:36:51,801
I don't believe it. They
were gonna kill me.

526
00:36:52,310 --> 00:36:55,075
Mr. Matlock's pretty smart
getting them to follow him like that.

527
00:36:55,246 --> 00:36:57,442
He's gonna get
you out of here, Dad.

528
00:36:57,615 --> 00:36:59,015
I owe you one, boy.

529
00:36:59,184 --> 00:37:02,245
When this is over with, I'm gonna
take you anywhere you wanna go.

530
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:05,879
- Hawaii, California, Mexico.
- Cancun?

531
00:37:06,357 --> 00:37:09,088
They got fine women
in Mexico, Matt.

532
00:37:17,869 --> 00:37:19,770
Yeah, I brought the kid
down to see his father.

533
00:37:19,938 --> 00:37:21,668
Yeah, I heard Ben
was Joe's lawyer.

534
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:23,520
I tell you though, I
was kind of surprised.

535
00:37:23,675 --> 00:37:26,611
- Doesn't seem like his kind of case.
- What makes you say that?

536
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:28,406
Well, the guy's a bum.

537
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:30,674
Well, they say you stay in
this business long enough,

538
00:37:30,849 --> 00:37:32,943
- you handle them all.
- Maybe you're right.

539
00:37:38,790 --> 00:37:40,952
Hello, Becky.

540
00:37:41,126 --> 00:37:43,357
You know, you only
made that one mistake.

541
00:37:43,528 --> 00:37:46,259
The only time Willie Roach ever
had somebody collect the money

542
00:37:46,431 --> 00:37:49,060
from the tellers was the
time he robbed your bank.

543
00:37:49,234 --> 00:37:51,567
Well, that doesn't prove
anything. You have no evidence.

544
00:37:51,736 --> 00:37:53,295
That's not what they tell me.

545
00:37:53,471 --> 00:37:56,464
Besides, only somebody who had been
at that robbery would have known that.

546
00:37:56,641 --> 00:37:58,161
And you were there,
weren't you, Becky?

547
00:37:58,309 --> 00:38:01,245
You're the only one that still
works at the bank that was there.

548
00:38:02,347 --> 00:38:03,371
Okay, we're out of here.

549
00:38:04,315 --> 00:38:05,715
Bye.

550
00:38:09,988 --> 00:38:11,786
Six cents.

551
00:38:12,457 --> 00:38:14,688
Three of a kind beats two
pair. A full house beats...

552
00:38:14,859 --> 00:38:17,090
I know. I know.

553
00:38:18,596 --> 00:38:21,498
- I fold.
- Nothing. Not even a pair.

554
00:38:21,666 --> 00:38:24,795
You know, I don't even
have to cheat to beat you.

555
00:38:25,737 --> 00:38:27,535
Game is not
over until it's over.

556
00:38:27,705 --> 00:38:30,072
In that case, you maybe
wanna play for more money?

557
00:38:30,241 --> 00:38:32,540
- Hey, you guys.
- Oh, hey, Jerr.

558
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:35,305
Doc Holliday here
is hustling me.

559
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:37,676
Man, it's like taking
candy from a baby.

560
00:38:37,849 --> 00:38:39,909
Don't get cocky, kid.

561
00:38:40,919 --> 00:38:45,855
- Right.
- I... How's about 10 cents?

562
00:38:49,427 --> 00:38:50,588
I call you.

563
00:38:50,762 --> 00:38:52,856
You don't have to say, "I
call you." Just say "call."

564
00:38:53,031 --> 00:38:54,397
Call.

565
00:38:54,766 --> 00:38:57,861
- How many cards you want?
- Um, think I'll take two.

566
00:38:58,036 --> 00:39:01,165
Two. Put them down
there. Deuce, down and dirty.

567
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,433
Dealer takes one.

568
00:39:03,741 --> 00:39:04,936
Okay.

569
00:39:07,045 --> 00:39:13,212
Let's go up, uh,
how about 17 cents?

570
00:39:16,254 --> 00:39:17,483
I fold.

571
00:39:17,655 --> 00:39:19,419
I told you I'd take
you to the cleaners.

572
00:39:19,591 --> 00:39:22,220
Better man won. Go to bed.

573
00:39:22,393 --> 00:39:24,794
All right. Well, anytime you
wanna play, just give me a call.

574
00:39:24,963 --> 00:39:29,059
- Okay.
- All right. Good night.

575
00:39:29,234 --> 00:39:30,668
Good night.

576
00:39:31,502 --> 00:39:33,164
Sleep tight.

577
00:39:36,241 --> 00:39:39,075
You had a full house. Why
didn't you stay in the game?

578
00:39:39,244 --> 00:39:40,371
Oh, we had a deal.

579
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:42,741
When one of us won a
dollar, he would go to bed.

580
00:39:50,822 --> 00:39:54,418
Say, uh, Jerr, wanna sit
down and play a hand?

581
00:39:55,493 --> 00:39:56,825
No.

582
00:39:56,995 --> 00:39:59,965
All right. Hey, I'm glad you're
here. I had to talk to you.

583
00:40:00,131 --> 00:40:01,929
- About what?
- Well, I tracked down

584
00:40:02,100 --> 00:40:06,435
the owner of that stolen Jaguar
that we found over at the chop shop.

585
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:07,902
Yeah.

586
00:40:08,773 --> 00:40:12,403
Guy was out of the country.
Didn't even know his car was stolen.

587
00:40:13,244 --> 00:40:15,907
- Does he know Joe Ahern?
- No, he doesn't.

588
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:20,108
But he has been to Plato's and
the passenger door was broken into.

589
00:40:21,185 --> 00:40:25,452
So both the owners of the stolen cars
have been to where Joe Ahern works?

590
00:40:30,762 --> 00:40:33,857
I got a sick feeling in
the pit of my stomach.

591
00:40:34,465 --> 00:40:37,162
- Yeah.
- Poor kid.

592
00:40:39,470 --> 00:40:42,872
Well, he's smart, I guess.

593
00:40:43,041 --> 00:40:46,273
Streetwise. I don't know.

594
00:40:46,711 --> 00:40:48,737
He's a good kid.

595
00:40:49,013 --> 00:40:50,709
He's a thief.

596
00:40:51,149 --> 00:40:53,550
You're a lawyer. Your
daughter's a lawyer.

597
00:40:53,718 --> 00:40:57,018
His father is a thief.
What do you expect?

598
00:40:57,789 --> 00:40:59,655
I suppose.

599
00:40:59,824 --> 00:41:03,090
You're his role model.
He looks up to you.

600
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:05,559
You hear the way he talks to me?

601
00:41:05,730 --> 00:41:09,633
Look, all I'm saying
is that he thinks

602
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:12,270
you're smart and he knows
that you're good at what you do.

603
00:41:12,437 --> 00:41:16,067
And that's why he's so hell-bent
on you representing his dad.

604
00:41:16,674 --> 00:41:19,234
Well, I'm not his dad. Ha, ha.

605
00:41:20,445 --> 00:41:24,974
Dealing with a 12-year-old boy
day-to-day, especially that one...

606
00:41:25,550 --> 00:41:27,644
Think we're actually
gonna find anything in here?

607
00:41:27,819 --> 00:41:29,651
You never know.

608
00:41:30,254 --> 00:41:31,415
Ah.

609
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:33,357
Mm.

610
00:41:38,730 --> 00:41:40,028
Ew.

611
00:41:52,043 --> 00:41:56,276
The owners of the Porsche
and Jaguar both went to Plato's.

612
00:41:56,447 --> 00:41:58,211
- It's a coincidence.
- Maybe.

613
00:41:58,383 --> 00:42:03,447
I found this under the dash
of that stolen Honda Prelude.

614
00:42:04,722 --> 00:42:06,452
- Chewing gum?
- Yeah.

615
00:42:06,624 --> 00:42:09,321
The police are
doing a DNA test on it

616
00:42:09,494 --> 00:42:12,362
but you and I know
how it's gonna turn out.

617
00:42:12,597 --> 00:42:15,157
It might be best if
you talk to the boy.

618
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:30,712
- Hey, Dad.
- Hey, son.

619
00:42:32,050 --> 00:42:34,530
Dad, look at these hotels in
Cancun. They got everything there.

620
00:42:34,685 --> 00:42:35,845
- I'm telling you.
- Sit down.

621
00:42:35,987 --> 00:42:37,747
We can learn how to
go snorkeling with tanks.

622
00:42:37,889 --> 00:42:40,154
Please, sit down.

623
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:44,461
Is something wrong?

624
00:42:48,666 --> 00:42:50,225
I wanna thank you
for all you've done.

625
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:53,769
- Dad, you already did that.
- Let me speak, please.

626
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:57,170
You're not gonna
make this easy, are you?

627
00:42:57,775 --> 00:42:59,573
Dad, what's wrong?

628
00:43:00,978 --> 00:43:03,641
I wanna thank you
for believing in me.

629
00:43:03,815 --> 00:43:07,843
You went out, you got Ben Matlock
and you convinced him to defend me.

630
00:43:08,386 --> 00:43:11,015
A father couldn't ask
for more from a son.

631
00:43:11,889 --> 00:43:13,755
There's just one problem.

632
00:43:13,925 --> 00:43:15,257
I'm guilty, Matt.

633
00:43:16,994 --> 00:43:18,895
But I thought you
said you didn't do it.

634
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:21,724
- I lied.
- You said we'd never lie to each other.

635
00:43:21,866 --> 00:43:23,767
Maybe to other people,
but never to each other.

636
00:43:23,935 --> 00:43:28,498
Matt, I'm a thief. I'm not somebody
you ought to be looking up to.

637
00:43:30,508 --> 00:43:33,205
And I believed you when
you said you didn't do it.

638
00:43:36,147 --> 00:43:37,581
I know.

639
00:43:41,486 --> 00:43:44,422
I'm trying to tell
you I'm going to jail.

640
00:43:45,456 --> 00:43:47,652
No, no, you're not. Ben
Matlock will get you off.

641
00:43:47,825 --> 00:43:49,726
- No, he won't.
- Yes, he will.

642
00:43:49,894 --> 00:43:51,954
I had an arrangement
with him. He'll get you off.

643
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:54,090
- I'm gonna talk to him right now.
- Listen to me.

644
00:43:55,199 --> 00:43:57,600
Ben Matlock and I
have already talked.

645
00:43:57,768 --> 00:44:00,966
Now, I'm going to jail,
Matt, for maybe two years.

646
00:44:02,773 --> 00:44:05,106
There's one good thing
that can come out of all this.

647
00:44:07,311 --> 00:44:09,644
I want you to learn
not to be like me.

648
00:44:09,814 --> 00:44:11,646
I don't want you to be a thief.

649
00:44:11,816 --> 00:44:14,308
I don't want you
to wind up in jail.

650
00:44:14,485 --> 00:44:15,851
You're a good kid.

651
00:44:16,020 --> 00:44:17,540
You can do better
than me. You hear me?

652
00:44:18,156 --> 00:44:20,182
I don't want you
to go to jail, Dad.

653
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:24,085
I know.

654
00:44:31,903 --> 00:44:34,532
How come you never
told me about your uncle?

655
00:44:34,705 --> 00:44:36,640
I don't wanna stay at his house.

656
00:44:36,807 --> 00:44:40,005
Your father says
he's a good guy.

657
00:44:40,178 --> 00:44:42,170
Yeah, well, maybe,
but there's no fun.

658
00:44:42,346 --> 00:44:44,406
He's always lecturing
me about junk,

659
00:44:44,582 --> 00:44:48,451
telling me to go to bed early,
never lets me cut school.

660
00:44:48,619 --> 00:44:50,281
I think I'd like him.

661
00:44:50,454 --> 00:44:52,374
Yeah, how would you like
an old coot with glasses

662
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:54,651
staring at you all the time?

663
00:44:55,359 --> 00:44:58,022
I don't know how to answer that.

664
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:02,133
Well, could be he
doesn't trust you.

665
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:05,867
You need to make him trust
you. Give you more freedom.

666
00:45:06,037 --> 00:45:08,268
- And maybe hell will freeze over.
- Ha, ha.

667
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:10,780
How come I can't stay with you?

668
00:45:12,243 --> 00:45:14,303
You wouldn't like it here.

669
00:45:14,946 --> 00:45:16,506
It would be a lot
better than Uncle Bob.

670
00:45:17,582 --> 00:45:22,486
I'm sorry, Matt, but I'm past getting
kids off to school and making lunches.

671
00:45:22,653 --> 00:45:25,248
- Been there, done that, huh?
- Yep, yep.

672
00:45:25,423 --> 00:45:30,418
But I tell you, if you wanna come hang
around some weekend, give me a call.

673
00:45:30,595 --> 00:45:32,029
Deal.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
